Code taken from the ASP.NET Web Stack is in the external/AspNetWebStack submodule (https://github.com/xforcore/AspNetWebStack,
branch webforcore), compiled by the src/ and test/ projects listed for it in the summary above. Each file keeps its
original copyright header; every change is a commit on that branch, with its reason (docs/MODIFICATIONS.md).

The assemblies built from that code are delay signed with Microsoft's public key
(src/SigningKey/35MSSharedLib1024.snk, from the ASP.NET Web Stack repository), so that their
identity matches the assemblies Microsoft ships. They are not signed by Microsoft.

This product includes software from Katana (https://github.com/aspnet/AspNetKatana, commit 096e225), licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt), with the same notice as above. It is in
the external/AspNetKatana submodule (https://github.com/xforcore/AspNetKatana, branch webforcore), compiled by
src/webForCore.Microsoft.Owin* and test/webForCore.Microsoft.Owin*; each file keeps its original copyright header, and
every change is a commit on that branch. Those assemblies are delay signed with the same Microsoft public key and carry
Microsoft.Owin's version 4.2.3.0. webForCore's own files in those projects say so in their header.

This product includes tests from Mono (https://github.com/mono/mono, mcs/class/System.Web/Test and
mcs/class/test-helpers, commit 0f53e9e), licensed under the MIT License. Each file keeps its original copyright
header (for example "Copyright (C) 2005 Novell, Inc (http://www.novell.com)") and MIT permission notice. They are in
the external/mono submodule (https://github.com/xforcore/mono, branch webforcore), compiled by
test/webForCore.System.Web.MonoTests; every change is a commit on that branch.
Files without their own header (test-helpers/NunitHelpers.cs) are covered by Mono's repository LICENSE, which
places the class libraries under the MIT License.

